Add the Quickshell.Wayland PresentationFeedback attached type: per-frame
wp_presentation feedback for a window. frameSwapped says only that Qt queued
a frame; VGS starts the Jarvis review pause on a frame the compositor
presented. VGS-only: upstream has no issue or PR; required by
docs/architecture/distribution.md § Quickshell engine.

Hyprland 0.57.2 (protocols/PresentationTime.cpp, protocols/core/Compositor.cpp,
render/pass/Pass.cpp, output/OutputCommitCoordinator.cpp) sends presented once
it drew the surface's committed state into an output frame the backend reports
presented. It sends discarded when a later buffer supersedes that state, when
the surface is not drawn (fully covered by opaque content, no texture, empty or
clipped away), when the output commit fails or is dropped, when the monitor is
removed and when the surface is destroyed. presented proves light on that
output, not that no other surface covered part of the window.

